1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,966
In Seoul, an evening lesson can
run into a citywide time limit.

2
00:00:04,966 --> 00:00:10,720
For school curriculum hagwons, the
permitted teaching hours end at 10 PM.

3
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:14,976
A classroom timetable has
to fit inside that boundary.

4
00:00:15,426 --> 00:00:18,284
This can happen after a full school day.

5
00:00:18,284 --> 00:00:23,787
A separate provider, in a separate
building, offers another scheduled lesson.

6
00:00:23,787 --> 00:00:28,146
Korea calls this kind of private
teaching institute a hagwon.

7
00:00:28,596 --> 00:00:30,900
Follow an illustrative evening.

8
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:34,467
School finishes, a paid
lesson begins elsewhere,

9
00:00:34,467 --> 00:00:37,886
and another set of tasks
enters the timetable.

10
00:00:37,886 --> 00:00:42,420
The same day can contain several
distinct learning schedules.

11
00:00:42,870 --> 00:00:44,569
Hagwon is a broad term.

12
00:00:44,569 --> 00:00:48,705
This episode follows the
school curriculum side, using a

13
00:00:48,705 --> 00:00:53,358
fictional mathematics course to
show how the arrangement works.

14
00:00:53,808 --> 00:00:57,718
The 10 PM limit in this
episode is Seoul's rule.

15
00:00:57,718 --> 00:01:04,152
Local regulations matter, so a timetable
in another region needs its own check.

16
00:01:04,602 --> 00:01:09,313
The broader sector includes different
subjects and learning goals.

17
00:01:09,313 --> 00:01:12,525
A language lesson, an
arts course, and school

18
00:01:12,525 --> 00:01:15,666
subject support can
have different purposes.

19
00:01:16,116 --> 00:01:20,738
The classroom can occupy part of
an ordinary commercial building.

20
00:01:20,738 --> 00:01:23,867
A street full of
businesses can also contain

21
00:01:23,867 --> 00:01:27,138
scheduled learning behind
upper floor windows.

22
00:01:27,138 --> 00:01:31,404
Education becomes one use among
several within the building.

23
00:01:31,854 --> 00:01:35,959
Signs and lit windows can
suggest a learning district.

24
00:01:35,959 --> 00:01:40,369
To understand a particular
course, we need to go past that

25
00:01:40,369 --> 00:01:45,006
street image and look at its
subject, schedule, and operator.

26
00:01:45,456 --> 00:01:50,666
An operator must register a hagwon
with the education authorities.

27
00:01:50,666 --> 00:01:54,377
The registration includes
information about the

28
00:01:54,377 --> 00:01:58,008
curriculum, instructors,
fees, and facilities.

29
00:01:58,458 --> 00:02:02,672
That makes the course a separate
service with its own operator.

30
00:02:02,672 --> 00:02:05,950
Enrolling connects a
household to that particular

31
00:02:05,950 --> 00:02:08,826
service for an agreed
learning arrangement.

32
00:02:09,276 --> 00:02:13,235
Our fictional course provides
weekly mathematics sessions.

33
00:02:13,235 --> 00:02:17,741
The timetable specifies when to
arrive, and the course description

34
00:02:17,741 --> 00:02:21,564
explains what the lessons
will cover during that period.

35
00:02:22,014 --> 00:02:28,195
A course might organize learning by grade,
by subject level, or by a particular goal.

36
00:02:28,195 --> 00:02:34,086
A lesson focused on review has a different
starting point from advanced practice.

37
00:02:34,536 --> 00:02:37,963
An explanation introduces
an idea, practice

38
00:02:37,963 --> 00:02:41,549
tests its use, and
feedback reveals mistakes.

39
00:02:41,549 --> 00:02:45,294
A later lesson can return
to those mistakes and

40
00:02:45,294 --> 00:02:48,960
build on what the learner
already understands.

41
00:02:49,410 --> 00:02:51,857
Imagine a lesson about fractions.

42
00:02:51,857 --> 00:02:55,490
The course can spend time
on an explanation, work

43
00:02:55,490 --> 00:02:59,345
through examples, and then
set independent practice.

44
00:02:59,345 --> 00:03:02,682
That is how the booked
teaching time is used.

45
00:03:03,132 --> 00:03:08,122
Repeated meetings allow an instructor
to revisit earlier material.

46
00:03:08,122 --> 00:03:11,448
A course built around
one subject can devote

47
00:03:11,448 --> 00:03:15,228
several meetings to a skill
that still needs work.

48
00:03:15,678 --> 00:03:20,645
A different course might prepare material
that will appear later at school.

49
00:03:20,645 --> 00:03:24,222
The sequence depends on that
course’s particular goal.

50
00:03:24,672 --> 00:03:29,402
Each option takes a subject, a
level, and a portion of the week.

51
00:03:29,402 --> 00:03:34,944
A household chooses a combination that
has to fit the rest of its schedule.

52
00:03:35,394 --> 00:03:39,010
The school timetable
already occupies part of it.

53
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:43,291
The hagwon lesson needs a start
time after the learner can

54
00:03:43,291 --> 00:03:47,202
leave school, travel, and
arrive at another building.

55
00:03:47,652 --> 00:03:51,637
A nearby lesson and a lesson
across town can use the same

56
00:03:51,637 --> 00:03:55,132
teaching period while
creating different evenings.

57
00:03:55,132 --> 00:03:59,676
The journey belongs in the schedule
alongside the classroom hour.

58
00:04:00,126 --> 00:04:05,447
Picture an illustrative session
starting at 7 PM and ending at 9 PM.

59
00:04:05,447 --> 00:04:08,029
That is 2 hours in the classroom.

60
00:04:08,029 --> 00:04:13,350
Getting there, eating, and getting
home still have to fit around it.

61
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:18,506
Those 2 hours can include
explanation, questions, and practice.

62
00:04:18,506 --> 00:04:22,166
A course timetable describes
the teaching period.

63
00:04:22,166 --> 00:04:25,527
The learner's evening
also includes the steps

64
00:04:25,527 --> 00:04:28,440
needed to reach that room and leave it.

65
00:04:28,890 --> 00:04:32,188
If the course assigns
work to complete at home,

66
00:04:32,188 --> 00:04:35,064
that work needs another place in the day.

67
00:04:35,064 --> 00:04:38,713
A lesson can end while tasks
connected to it remain.

68
00:04:38,713 --> 00:04:42,642
Homework joins whatever the
school has already assigned.

69
00:04:43,092 --> 00:04:45,946
A second course requires another slot.

70
00:04:45,946 --> 00:04:49,026
Adding one appointment can affect travel,

71
00:04:49,026 --> 00:04:52,406
meals, and the time left
between commitments.

72
00:04:52,406 --> 00:04:55,260
The whole schedule needs coordination.

73
00:04:55,710 --> 00:04:59,813
Seoul's education office
states that the teaching window

74
00:04:59,813 --> 00:05:03,696
for the covered institutions
runs from 5 AM to 10 PM.

75
00:05:03,696 --> 00:05:09,630
The education office links this boundary
to regular schooling and student health.

76
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:14,614
That boundary limits how late the
covered teaching can continue.

77
00:05:14,614 --> 00:05:17,307
A course that ends earlier has already

78
00:05:17,307 --> 00:05:20,424
finished before the
permitted window closes.

79
00:05:20,874 --> 00:05:24,783
We are following Seoul's school
curriculum teaching system.

80
00:05:24,783 --> 00:05:28,759
A different category of learning
facility can have different

81
00:05:28,759 --> 00:05:33,066
operating conditions, and a
different locality has its own rules.

82
00:05:33,516 --> 00:05:39,250
Seoul's guidance notes that an approved
extension can apply to that category.

83
00:05:39,250 --> 00:05:42,602
A room used for independent
study needs to be

84
00:05:42,602 --> 00:05:45,804
understood through its
own operating rules.

85
00:05:46,254 --> 00:05:49,803
The education office also
supervises compliance.

86
00:05:49,803 --> 00:05:55,793
Its guidance discusses checks on teaching
hours and other operating requirements.

87
00:05:55,793 --> 00:06:01,782
The time limit belongs to an enforceable
framework for the provider's activities.

88
00:06:02,232 --> 00:06:06,894
The law requires providers to
display relevant fees and refund

89
00:06:06,894 --> 00:06:11,330
information, and to issue
receipts when fees are collected.

90
00:06:11,330 --> 00:06:16,368
A paid lesson brings a transaction
alongside the learning schedule.

91
00:06:16,818 --> 00:06:21,922
For the household, those details connect
a payment to a particular course.

92
00:06:21,922 --> 00:06:25,025
The timetable tells it
when teaching happens.

93
00:06:25,025 --> 00:06:29,922
The fee information tells it what is
being charged for the arrangement.

94
00:06:30,372 --> 00:06:32,081
Another cost is time.

95
00:06:32,081 --> 00:06:35,824
An evening contains a
limited number of hours.

96
00:06:35,824 --> 00:06:39,973
A lesson, its travel, and
any assigned practice all

97
00:06:39,973 --> 00:06:43,716
draw on the same available
stretch of the day.

98
00:06:44,166 --> 00:06:48,941
That creates a practical tradeoff
with rest and unstructured time.

99
00:06:48,941 --> 00:06:53,643
Adding an appointment uses a slot
that could hold something else.

100
00:06:53,643 --> 00:06:55,958
The effect depends on the actual

101
00:06:55,958 --> 00:06:59,286
timetable, travel distance,
and work assigned.

102
00:06:59,736 --> 00:07:02,579
Coordination can extend to the household.

103
00:07:02,579 --> 00:07:05,144
Meals, pickup arrangements, and other

104
00:07:05,144 --> 00:07:08,611
appointments may have to
be matched to the lesson.

105
00:07:08,611 --> 00:07:11,869
The course can be a single
booking with several

106
00:07:11,869 --> 00:07:14,712
consequences for the surrounding evening.

107
00:07:15,162 --> 00:07:17,807
There can also be a gap between buying

108
00:07:17,807 --> 00:07:20,800
teaching and obtaining
a particular result.

109
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:24,490
A course supplies organized
instruction and practice.

110
00:07:24,490 --> 00:07:28,040
What a learner understands
afterwards still depends

111
00:07:28,040 --> 00:07:31,242
on how those activities
work for that learner.

112
00:07:31,692 --> 00:07:35,141
Different course choices
produce different weeks.

113
00:07:35,141 --> 00:07:38,591
One arrangement might add
a short review session.

114
00:07:38,591 --> 00:07:41,336
Another might combine several subjects.

115
00:07:41,336 --> 00:07:44,644
The institutional system
supplies options while

116
00:07:44,644 --> 00:07:48,516
individual timetables vary
from household to household.

117
00:07:48,966 --> 00:07:54,772
A course offers scheduled attention to a
defined subject, a sequence of practice,

118
00:07:54,772 --> 00:07:59,862
and opportunities to get feedback
outside the regular school timetable.

119
00:08:00,312 --> 00:08:04,154
Put several such services
close together and learning

120
00:08:04,154 --> 00:08:07,996
also becomes part of a
neighborhood's daily movement.

121
00:08:07,996 --> 00:08:11,475
Buildings, routes, and
appointment times connect

122
00:08:11,475 --> 00:08:14,592
the home to a market
of teaching providers.

123
00:08:15,042 --> 00:08:17,786
The system has several linked layers.

124
00:08:17,786 --> 00:08:22,236
Registration identifies the
provider, the course defines the

125
00:08:22,236 --> 00:08:26,908
service, the timetable allocates
teaching time, and local rules

126
00:08:26,908 --> 00:08:30,690
set boundaries around how
that service can operate.

127
00:08:31,140 --> 00:08:36,288
That explains why a clock can be a
powerful introduction to hagwons.

128
00:08:36,288 --> 00:08:39,090
A lesson is part of education, a paid

129
00:08:39,090 --> 00:08:42,345
service, and a scheduled
use of a building.

130
00:08:42,345 --> 00:08:45,828
The same clock touches
all of those functions.

131
00:08:46,278 --> 00:08:49,645
At the end of the fictional
evening, the course

132
00:08:49,645 --> 00:08:52,511
has finished and the learner heads home.

133
00:08:52,511 --> 00:08:55,233
Travel continues after teaching stops.

134
00:08:55,233 --> 00:09:00,606
Any work assigned for home follows its
own place in the remaining schedule.

135
00:09:01,056 --> 00:09:05,498
The arrangement becomes clearer
when we follow the whole chain.

136
00:09:05,498 --> 00:09:10,505
A household books a course, the
provider teaches at an agreed time, and

137
00:09:10,505 --> 00:09:14,736
the learner carries the experience
into the rest of the day.

138
00:09:15,186 --> 00:09:19,875
What does the course teach, when
does it meet, how is it paid for, and

139
00:09:19,875 --> 00:09:24,162
how much of the evening does the
whole arrangement actually use?

140
00:09:24,612 --> 00:09:27,333
Return to the lit windows in Seoul.

141
00:09:27,333 --> 00:09:32,621
Behind each one can be a different
subject, timetable, and provider.

142
00:09:32,621 --> 00:09:36,275
The 10 PM boundary gives
us an entry point into

143
00:09:36,275 --> 00:09:39,852
that much larger system
of scheduled learning.

144
00:09:40,302 --> 00:09:45,143
Hagwons turn a portion of the week
into a bookable learning service.

145
00:09:45,143 --> 00:09:48,418
Understanding that
arrangement means following

146
00:09:48,418 --> 00:09:51,408
both the classroom and the time around it.

147
00:09:51,408 --> 00:09:52,974
This is Only in Korea.
